  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes the outcomes relative to a reference (zero), their differences, and the probabilities of those differences. The individual considered the outcomes (2500 vs. 2400) and their probabilities, especially focusing on the chance of getting zero, which is directly related to the chance of getting a positive difference from the reference. The justification aligns with evaluating the favorable differences from zero (the reference) and their likelihoods. Although the individual does not explicitly calculate mean differences, their focus on both higher gains and lower chances of zero reflects a consideration of the expected magnitude of gains above the reference (zero), which is the core of the decision reason. The reasoning pattern matches the rule of the decision reason, even if not formalized. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
